title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Payment checks: authorization to other insurance
route: /authorizations/eligibility/R-1042
intro: Rows 4 to 7 of 'Payment checks' (in the side panel 'Verification details'). What the patient pays is not in this list: it is its own row, 'Patient pays', on the result (and in the panel's summary when opened from New Case). Authorization is the only row that can turn the verdict amber. The others turn it red.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: 'Limit reached' has a seeded patient (R-0921) and 'Another plan pays first' has one (I-2275). Both have a chip under 'Try a sample' on Verify.
---
start s1 "Result page, side panel opened, 'Payment checks', rows 4 to 7"
decision q9 "Was coverage found?"
endx x9 "Coverage not found\nRows 2 to 7 are not shown\nOne grey row says nothing else could be checked"

group gA "Row 4 · Authorization"
  decision a0 "What is the authorization state?"
  process a1 "Chip 'Not required' (green)\n'Beacon does not require one for IOP'"
  process a2 "Chip 'On file' (green)\n'On file with Summit. 9 of 14 days used'"
  process a3 "Chip 'Required' (amber)\n'Required before the first day. A request is being drafted'"
  process a4 "Chip 'Under review' (amber)\n'Required. Under review with Cardinal'"
  process a5 "Chip 'Retro request open' (amber)\n'Retro-authorization request open, for days already delivered'"
  process a6 "Chip 'Required' (amber)\n'Required before the first day. Not on file'"
  process a7 "Chip 'Unknown' (grey)\n'No rule on file for Beacon and residential 3.5. Nothing was assumed'\nThe check could not run, so it is not counted as a failure"
endgroup

group gB "Row 5 · Can the clinic bill?"
  decision b0 "Is the clinic enrolled with this payer for this level of care?"
  process b1 "Title 'The clinic can bill', chip 'In network' (green)\n'Enrolled and in network with Summit for residential 3.5'"
  process b2 "Title 'The clinic cannot bill yet', chip 'Not enrolled' (red)\n'Not enrolled with Evergreen for detox'"
  process b3 "Title 'The clinic's enrollment is not confirmed', chip 'Not confirmed' (amber)\n'Enrollment with Lakeshore for IOP could not be confirmed'\nThe result offers 'Ask Navigator to check enrollment'"
endgroup

group gC "Row 6 · Limits"
  decision c0 "Is there a day or unit limit?"
  process c1 "Chip '5 days left' (green), or amber at 3 or fewer\n'9 of 14 days used in this authorization period'"
  process c2 "Title 'Every authorized day is used' (or unit)\nChip 'Limit reached' (red)\n'14 of 14 days used in this authorization period'"
  process c3 "Chip 'No limit' (green)\n'No annual day limit for residential 3.5'\nor 'No visit or day limit for this program'"
endgroup

group gD "Row 7 · Other insurance"
  decision d0 "Did the check find another plan?"
  process d1 "Title 'No other insurance', chip 'None' (green)\n'None found'"
  process d2 "Title 'Another plan pays first', chip 'Other plan' (red)\n'A second plan was found. It is billed before this one'"
endgroup

group gP "What the patient pays (not a payment check)"
  decision p0 "Does the plan type have a cost share on file?"
  process p1 "Row 'Patient pays' on the result\nHarborview 'Deductible $85 left, coinsurance 20%'\nBeacon and Lakeshore 'Copay $40 per day, deductible $350 left, coinsurance 20% after the deductible'"
  process p3 "Ohio Medicaid: no row at all\nNo '$0 copay' text, because members usually pay none"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Patient, insurance and request rows"
s1 --> q9
q9 -->|No| x9
q9 -->|Yes| a0
a0 -->|Not required| a1 --> b0
a0 -->|On file| a2 --> b0
a0 -->|Being drafted| a3 --> b0
a0 -->|With the payer| a4 --> b0
a0 -->|Retro request| a5 --> b0
a0 -->|Required, not started| a6 --> b0
a0 -->|No rule on file| a7 --> b0
b0 -->|Yes| b1 --> c0
b0 -->|No| b2 --> c0
b0 -->|Could not confirm| b3 --> c0
c0 -->|Limit, room left| c1 --> d0
c0 -->|Limit, none left| c2 --> d0
c0 -->|No limit| c3 --> d0
d0 -->|No| d1 --> p0
d0 -->|Yes| d2 --> p0
p0 -->|Yes| p1 --> g1
p0 -->|No| p3 --> g1
